How to make Obj's `__dict__` unavailable for this class while retaining instance attrs? The instance attributes in our Obj are stored in `AStore` (either inline attrs or dict after `__dict__` read). `getattr` special case returns `ob.dict()` when class has no `__dict__`. If we set a class attribute `__dict__` that is a property raising AttributeError, then `hasattr` False and `vi.__dict__` raises. But instance `setattr` may interact. Let's explore dynpy's Obj internals to see whether setting a class-level `__dict__` property would be safe and whether `repr` closure's `o.get` still works.

`getattr` V::Obj:
```rust
if name == "__dict__" && ob.cls.lookup(name).is_none() {
    return ob.dict();
}
if let Some(v) = ob.get_attr(name)? { return Ok(v); }
if let Some(v) = ob.cls.lookup(name) {
    return match &v {
        V::Func(f) => ...
        V::Prop(p) => call(&p.0, Args::p(vec![o.clone()])),
        _ => Ok(v),
    };
}
```
If class attr `__dict__` is a V::Prop with getter function that returns Err(AttributeError with full message), getattr will call and raise. Good.

What about `type(vi).__dict__`? V::Class branch:
```rust
if let Some(v) = c.lookup(name) { return Ok(match &v { V::Func ... _ => v}); }
```
It returns the Prop itself, so `print(type(vi).__dict__)` would print `<property object>` instead of mappingproxy. CPython prints mappingproxy. But hidden tests may not print class __dict__. Could we make class attr `__dict__` a V::View mappingproxy and also have instance getattr raise? Not easily: class lookup returns V::View to instance getattr too, no raise. Need a property that raises for instance but class access special-cased? V::Class branch could return mappingproxy if name == "__dict__" and c.name == "version_info"... too special-case.

Alternative: change `getattr` V::Obj special case to look at class's `__slots__` or a flag rather than class `__dict__`, and leave class branch generating mappingproxy. Add a new Class field `has_instance_dict: Cell<bool>` defaulting true; set false for this class. Then getattr checks `if name == "__dict__" && ob.cls.lookup(name).is_none() && ob.cls.has_instance_dict()` else falls to normal error. But error message would `'version_info' object has no attribute '__dict__'` (still module mismatch), and `hasattr` False. Also `ob.dict()` elsewhere? Search uses of `.dict()`.

